<http://data.silknow.org/object/0b4eb3ae-b386-3390-bd29-477496d4266c>
        a                              ecrm:E22_Man-Made_Object ;
        rdfs:comment                   "Pair of sleeves made from machine-made net, England, 1815-1825"@en , "Pair of sleeves made from white machine-made net. Full length and tapering towards the wrist, gathered at regular intervals onto a cord, and these puffs are held by lengths of cord stitched the length of the sleeve. At the top they have white silk ribbons for attachments to the dress and at the wrist a white cut carrickmacross-work cuff."@en ;
        ecrm:P138i_has_representation  <http://data.silknow.org/image/5711e16d-2b0f-341f-be75-dd5b6bb65a4c> , <http://data.silknow.org/image/37d91f35-4327-3d03-8661-8299dc1e8c53> ;
